      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/la_cisterna",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Established on 30 May 1925, La Cisterna transitioned from rural plots to a formal commune.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/la_cisterna",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "La Cisterna sits between the coastal range and Andean foothills, giving it a flat, stable landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/la_cisterna",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The commune averages 360 mm of rain yearly, mostly in winter, while summers stay dry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/la_cisterna",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Despite dense urbanization, La Cisterna hosts 51 green spots, including Parque Cívico and Plaza Los Bomberos.",
